<article class="env-lemma" id="D311">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/D311">Lemma <span data-tag="D311">6.1.3.17</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-category, and let $U_{\bullet }: \Nerve (\cDelta )^{op} \rightarrow \calX $ be a simplicial object of $\calX $. Let $U'_{\bullet }$ be the augmented simplicial object given by composing $U_{\bullet }$ with the functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \cDelta _{+} \rightarrow \cDelta  \]
</div>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  J \rightarrow J \amalg \{  \infty \} . \]
</div>
  <p> Then: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The augmented simplicial object $U'_{\bullet }$ is a colimit diagram. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
If $U_{\bullet }$ is a groupoid object of $\calX $, then the evident natural transformation of simplicial objects $\alpha : U'_{\bullet } | \Nerve (\cDelta )^{op} \rightarrow U_{\bullet }$ is Cartesian. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assertion $(1)$ follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/4CC3" data-tag="4CC3">6.1.3.16</a>. To prove $(2)$, let us consider the collection $S$ of all morphisms $f: J \rightarrow J'$ in $\cDelta $ such that $\alpha (f)$ is a pullback square 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { U'_{\bullet }(J') \ar [r] \ar [d] &  U_{\bullet }(J') \ar [d] \\ U'_{\bullet }(J) \ar [r] &  U_{\bullet }(J) } \]
</div>
    <p>
       in $\calX $. We wish to prove that every morphism of $\cDelta $ belongs to $S$. Using Lemma <a href="/tag/ABC0" data-tag="ABC0">4.4.2.1</a>, we deduce that if $f' \in S$, then $f \in S \Leftrightarrow (f \circ f' \in S)$. Consequently, it will suffice to prove that every inclusion $\{ j\}  \subseteq J$ belongs to $S$. Unwinding the definition, this amounts the the requirement that the diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { U_{\bullet }( J \cup \{ \infty \}  ) \ar [d] \ar [r] &  U_{\bullet }( J) \ar [d] \\ U_{\bullet } ( \{ j, \infty \}  ) \ar [r] &  U_{\bullet }( \{ j\}  )} \]
</div>
    <p>
       is Cartesian, which follows immediately from Criterion $(4'')$ of Proposition <a href="/tag/D95F" data-tag="D95F">6.1.2.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>